Pantheon Digital — Building India's EPR Infrastructure, One Platform at a Time
Pantheon Digital Pvt. Ltd. was founded with one conviction: that India's environmental compliance landscape was broken — not because companies didn't want to comply, but because the tools to comply simply didn't exist. Regulators had built portals. Consultants offered advice. But no one had built the software layer that could sit between a company's internal operations and the CPCB portal — automating everything in between.
That gap was where Pantheon Digital chose to build.

Our Story
Founded
Pantheon Digital Pvt. Ltd. was incorporated as a technology company focused on regulatory compliance software for the Indian market. The founding team combined deep expertise in enterprise SaaS, Indian environmental law, and CPCB portal operations.
First product
EcoTrace — India's first fully automated EPR compliance platform — was built from the ground up as Pantheon Digital's flagship product. Unlike tools repurposed from other geographies or adapted from generic compliance software, EcoTrace was purpose-built for CPCB's specific workflows, certificate types, and filing formats.
First enterprise client
EcoTrace was first deployed for a leading FMCG enterprise — a pan-India company with plastic packaging obligations across multiple subsidiaries. This implementation shaped every module, every workflow, and every report that now powers EcoTrace.
From plastic to multi-category
After proving the model in plastic waste EPR, Pantheon Digital expanded EcoTrace to cover all five CPCB EPR categories: E-Waste, Battery Waste, Waste Tyre, and Used Oil — creating India's only unified, multi-category EPR compliance platform.
Today
EcoTrace serves clients across FMCG, pharma, electronics, automotive, and industrial sectors. Pantheon Digital is the only technology company in India to have built a production-grade, end-to-end EPR compliance platform across all five CPCB EPR categories.
Technology
Built on React.js (frontend), Spring Boot / Java (backend), PostgreSQL, and AWS Mumbai infrastructure — ensuring enterprise-grade security, DPDP Act 2023 compliance, and 99.5%+ uptime during compliance-critical periods.


